<title>NORWAY: Norway May CPI rises 0.3 pct mnth/mnth.</title>
<headline>Norway May CPI rises 0.3 pct mnth/mnth.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Norway (SSB) issued the following economic indicator.</p>
<p> NORWAY CONSUMER PRICES    MAY 1997   APRIL 1997   MAY 1996</p>
<p>  Figures (in percent)</p>
<p>  Month-on-month change	+0.3	  -0.1	  +0.2</p>
<p>  Year-on-year change	  +2.7	  +2.6	  +1.0</p>
<p>  Index (base 1979)	   269.7	 269.0	 262.6</p>
<p>NOTE -- Ten economists polled by Reuters forecast a year-on-year rise in May of 2.47 percent and for inflation to rise by 0.1 percent from April.</p>
<p>The government statistics office attributed the month-on-month rise mainly to higher prices of gasoline and foodstuffs. A decline in prices of clothes and electricity pulled in the opposite direction, it said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
